<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kertanegara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1275</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Kertanagara</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kertanegara was the last king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singhasari">Singhasari</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>. Around c. 1275 he launched a major military expedition against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a>, further weakening the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya Empire</a>. His defiance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kublai-khan">Kublai Khan</a> led to a Mongol expedition to Java, during which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit</a> emerged.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kertanegara.jpg" alt="Kertanegara" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anandajoti Bhikkhu from Sadao, Thailand · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:063_Main_Statue,_Joko_Dolog_(39706345204).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
